//? Title: Levinson recursion for symmetric Toeplitz systems
//? Subtitle: Actual prefix solves, the original8-by-8 system and explicit breakdown
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Constant diagonals let an unpivoted Toeplitz solver grow a solution one leading
order at a time in quadratic work. We inspect its actual forward/backward
vectors and error sums, retain the original8-by-8 example, compare against a
separate pivoted dense solver and expose a nonsingular matrix whose leading
block makes this recurrence break down. Finite output and a small residual do
not certify good conditioning or forward accuracy.
)

\toc

> Growing a leading system

A symmetric Toeplitz matrix is T(i,j)=r[abs(i−j)], entirely determined by its
first row. At leading order s, the recurrence maintains vectors f and b
satisfying T_s*f=e_first and T_s*b=e_last, plus the current solution x.
Extending to order s+1 produces three actual boundary error sums ef, eb and ex.
Padding f on the right and b on the left gives

$$f_{new}=\frac{f_{pad}-ef\,b_{pad}}{1-eb\,ef},\quad b_{new}=\frac{b_{pad}-eb\,f_{pad}}{1-eb\,ef},\quad x_{new}=x_{pad}+(rhs_s-ex)b_{new}.$$
\alttext(Actual forward and backward boundary errors update two inverse-column bases; the new residual correction extends the solution.)

Toeplitz shift structure makes the padded basis combination cancel every old
equation while correcting the new boundary equation. Starting with f=b=1/r0 and
x=rhs0/r0 proves the invariant inductively whenever each division is defined.
The denominator is an unpivoted leading-block requirement, not a full-matrix
singularity test. Positive definiteness avoids exact leading-block singularities
mathematically, but finite precision can still amplify error.

> Tiny actual extension

For row(2,1), rhs(1,1), the order1 basis is0.5, both boundary errors are0.5 and
the actual denominator is0.75. The new solution is(1/3,1/3). Every displayed
error, basis and solution below is captured from one producing native execution.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/levinson_extension.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/levinson.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::levinson_trace({2, 1}, {1, 1});
    auto e = t.attempts[0];
    std::print("| actual target order | actual forward error | actual backward error | actual solution " "error | actual denominator |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | " "{} |\n\n| actual solution index | actual final value |\n| ---: | ---: |\n",
               e.order, e.forward_error, e.backward_error, e.solution_error,
               e.denominator);
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.analysis.solution.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {:.12f} |\n", i, t.analysis.solution[i]);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("old", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual order1 bases\nf{}; b{}", t.states[0].forward[0],
                       t.states[0].backward[0])).node("errors", {6, 0},
                                                      std::format(
                                                      "Actual errors ef{}, eb{}\ndenominator{}",
                                                      e.forward_error,
                                                      e.backward_error,
                                                      e.denominator)).node(
        "new", {12, 0},
        std::format("Actual order2 solution\n{:.6f}, {:.6f}",
                    t.analysis.solution[0], t.analysis.solution[1])).edge(
        "old", "errors").edge("errors", "new").save_svg("build/levinson_extension.svg");
}
```
