> Contracts and verification

Complete row/rhs shapes and finite values are checked before indexing; both
empty is valid. Actual finite double operation order is preserved and nonfinite
produced arithmetic throws. Exact-zero initial diagonal or extension denominator
is explicit breakdown, with no arbitrary small-denominator tolerance. Negative
but nonsingular leading systems are allowed; no blanket positive-definiteness
claim is made. Scalar solve throws on breakdown; analysis/trace return the last
completed prefix and a false solved flag.

Full conservative trace admission counts2*n input values, sum over k=1..n
of(1+3*k) completed-state/vector records and n−1 possible attempts before
copying or computing. Actual captured_entries can be smaller on breakdown. The
million-entry default excludes scalar fields, capacities/output/runtime copies
and bytes/RAM;0 disables only the optional cap. States and inputs are owned and
come from one actual execution, with no repeated-prefix reconstruction. Widened
residual evaluation is additional O(n^2) work and does not certify forward
accuracy.

Independent NumPy dense solves and widened residual observations verified30
AR-shaped systems and1230 actual extension records; native tests separately
check every original8-by-8 prefix against pivoted solves and inverse-column
residuals, analytic AR inverse columns and the invertible full-matrix breakdown
control. Another500 ordinary systems matched the frozen solution vectors
bitwise. Shape/nonfinite/overflow, empty, conservative quota and ownership
controls pass; residuals remain observations rather than forward-error
certificates. The complete ten-report batch passed77 native CTest cases,39
directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases,106 compiled/executed public
examples,479/479 scoped definitions and ten representative clangd hovers. All4
complete report programs executed and all4 native figures were visually
reviewed. HTML/Markdown computed result and identical source/build/export figure
bytes passed verification. Repeatable receipts are retained under
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-194-203/`.

> References

N. Levinson,
[The Wiener(Root Mean Square) Error Criterion in Filter Design and Prediction|https://doi.org/10.1002/sapm1946251261],
Journal of Mathematics and Physics25,261–278. The publisher dates this
volume1946; the work is also commonly cited as1947. This implementation is an
unpivoted symmetric Toeplitz prefix recurrence, with its actual arithmetic and
breakdown domain stated explicitly rather than claiming universal numerical
stability.
